From dabf2442ea0adc4b145265e062d453149f633122 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:28:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: say in kodi.log why the metadata of a frame cannot
 be sent

When the serializer refused the metadata of a frame, nothing said which of
its thirty or so checks failed: DV_REQUIRE() returned false, the renderer
"render rejected stage=metadata-validation-or-reconstruction", and the log of
a title that lost native output had to be read against the code and the RPU.

Each check of the serializer that refuses a frame now names itself with a
fixed text (DV_REFUSE(): "two level 1 blocks", "the level 5 offsets leave no
picture", "the content mapping v2.9 part alone is over 512 bytes", "a
residual of the enhancement layer (FEL) that the picture was not drawn
with"...), and so do the checks of dvbridge_prepare_why() before it (the
place of the picture, metadata that do not read as FFmpeg lays them out).
dvbridge_prepare_transport() and dvbridge_prepare() stay as they were, for
their other callers. The renderer keeps the reason of its last render
(dvbridge_render_refused()), and CDVBridgeGLES writes each reason once a
stream, for the first eight reasons. A refusal of the source transport,
after which the frame goes out converted, is the reason that the log already
gives for that.

Nothing that is sent changes: the serializer host test prints the payload of
each of its 250 frames, and they are the same as before this change; its 21
new checks (each refusal and its reason) fail on the bridge before.
